{"id": "EUVD-2026-95021", "enisaUuid": "fafa8159-8dce-3518-bc69-3e549664db6a", "description": "Dislocker through 0.7.3 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in get_dataset() and get_next_datum() that never validate dataset and datum sizes against the metadata allocation. Attackers can craft a BitLocker volume image with inflated dataset or datum sizes that, when opened or mounted, crashes dislocker or discloses adjacent heap memory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T14:10:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-10T03:07:18", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Aorimn/dislocker/commit/9158e9e41dd669b360cbc53cc18ccae729b67b48", "https://github.com/Aorimn/dislocker/blob/v0.7.3/src/metadata/metadata.c#L764-L790", "https://github.com/Aorimn/dislocker/blob/v0.7.3/src/metadata/datums.c#L589-L640", "https://github.com/Aorimn/dislocker", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/dislocker-through-0.7.3-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-bitlocker-metadata-dataset-size"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-107634", "GHSA-gj99-98mp-m7r6"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ca35beaa-b290-32b9-bbbd-a1300f81c941", "product": {"name": "dislocker", "vendor": {"name": "Aorimn"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6429d69e-9855-356c-8fbf-a10248c4cd50", "vendor": {"name": "Aorimn"}}], "isExploited": false}